            <ArticleTitle>Linear scleroderma 'en coup de sabre' associated with cerebral and ocular vasculitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>402-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Linear scleroderma 'en coup de sabre' (LSCS) has been reported in association with intracranial abnormalities. We report the case of an 11-year-old boy with LSCS who presented with recurrent headaches. Cranial magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and angiography were consistent with the diagnosis of a cerebral vasculitis. In addition, retinal examination showed an exudative inflammatory lesion consistent with vasculitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
